{
  "diagnoses": [
    {
      "preserve": "Choose the appropriate FHIR version before installing a NuGet package or cloning the repository because HL7 specification updates introduce breaking changes.",
      "problem": "The warning buries its actionable point inside “it is important to understand” and “you need to ensure,” ending with the vague “right for you” before the concrete version list.",
      "quote": "Before installing one of the NuGet packages (or clone the repo) it is important to understand that HL7 has published several updates of the FHIR specification, each with breaking changes - so you need to ensure you use the version that is right for you:",
      "segment_index": 0,
      "unit_ordinal": 14
    },
    {
      "preserve": "The download must match the reader's FHIR release; retain the documentation reference.",
      "problem": "“The correct” lacks a noun, leaving the download instruction incomplete. The surrounding package discussion supplies the intended object.",
      "quote": ", and download the correct for your FHIR release.",
      "segment_index": 2,
      "unit_ordinal": 19
    },
    {
      "preserve": "The table below provides package links organized by FHIR version.",
      "problem": "This repeats the immediately preceding instruction to choose a download for the reader's FHIR release. Its only additional function is pointing to the table, which is obscured by another version-selection preamble.",
      "quote": "Depending on the version of FHIR you require, you'll find the relevant link to the package below.",
      "segment_index": 0,
      "unit_ordinal": 20
    },
    {
      "preserve": "Pre-release packages are public and can be used by adding the specified protected URL to NuGet sources; retain the distinction between release packages and packages produced by develop commits.",
      "problem": "“Want to be brave” adds an unsupported judgment about using pre-release packages, while “you can do so by” delays the actual setup instruction without describing a concrete caveat.",
      "quote": "These are public too. So if you want to be brave and use a pre-release packages, you can do so by adding",
      "segment_index": 0,
      "unit_ordinal": 30
    },
    {
      "preserve": "Maintaining compile compatibility between minor SDK releases is an effort rather than a guarantee; binary compatibility is explicitly excluded from that statement.",
      "problem": "“Spend a lot of effort” is an unquantified claim about maintainer effort that distracts from the compatibility policy readers need.",
      "quote": "We spend a lot of effort trying to maintain",
      "segment_index": 0,
      "unit_ordinal": 37
    },
    {
      "preserve": "The contact link is an invitation to inquire about the optional commercial support described immediately before it.",
      "problem": "“If this is relevant for you” and “feel free to” stack two layers of empty invitation framing around a contact action whose purpose is already established.",
      "quote": "If this is relevant for you, feel free to",
      "segment_index": 0,
      "unit_ordinal": 53
    },
    {
      "preserve": "The project uses Git Flow for branch management, and contribution PRs target the protected develop branch.",
      "problem": "The participation preamble repeats the Contributing section's purpose and grammatically makes the project's use of Git Flow sound conditional on the reader wanting to participate.",
      "quote": "If you want to participate in this project, we're using",
      "segment_index": 0,
      "unit_ordinal": 56
    },
    {
      "preserve": "The pipeline automatically checks binary compatibility and fails on breaks; exceptions are possible in some cases, and the protected command generates a suppression file locally.",
      "problem": "“In some cases” leaves the exception condition unspecified, while the following instruction presents suppression as a general way to prevent pipeline failure. The transition obscures that suppression belongs to the exception workflow. “The pipeline doesn't break” also blurs a compatibility-check failure with a malfunctioning pipeline.",
      "quote": "In some cases we can make an exception to break binary compatitibility. \nTo make sure the pipeline doesn't break, you should run",
      "segment_index": 0,
      "unit_ordinal": 59
    }
  ],
